01 cleo   cut   0.00-  6.78  speech   0.00-  5.52 | Claude, Chrome's gatekeeping. My API works in Postman. Here? CORS.
02 claude cut   6.78-  9.03  speech   7.26-  8.72 | Finally. Board time.
03 cleo   cut   9.03- 11.10  speech   9.18- 10.80 | Since when do you have a board?
04 claude cut  11.10- 17.27  speech  11.38- 17.20 | Since now. Your page: localhost, port three thousand. Your API: same host, port eight thousand.
05 cleo   cut  17.27- 19.66  speech  18.54- 19.26 | Same laptop.
06 claude cut  19.66- 24.92  speech  20.02- 24.82 | Different port, different origin. And Chrome checks the API's guest list.
07 cleo   cut  24.92- 27.50  speech  25.28- 27.16 | So Chrome blocks the request?
08 claude cut  27.50- 34.81  speech  27.76- 34.78 | Sometimes a preflight check stops it. Otherwise, Chrome hides the response unless your origin is on the list.
09 cleo   cut  34.81- 36.23  speech  35.38- 36.04 | And Postman?
10 claude cut  36.23- 40.68  speech  36.54- 40.30 | Postman isn't a browser. It never checks the guest list.
11 cleo   cut  40.68- 42.88  speech  40.72- 42.72 | So I fix it in the front end?
12 claude cut  42.88- 51.26  speech  43.34- 51.10 | Server side. Add Access-Control-Allow-Origin with your page's exact origin. Guests don't write the guest list.
13 cleo   cut  51.26- 55.98  speech  51.64- 55.60 | Allowed my page's exact origin on the server... It loaded!
